## Findings
Primary saved XML PMC11014456 Figure 8K-L supports EGR2 decay acceleration during CHX after 48 h db-cAMP induction, not merely a regulator-RNA correlation. Figure 8N reports MG132 recovery of EGR2 abundance without MPZ recovery. This changes the progenitor's proposed preference: EGR2 protein control is established source biology, but EGR2-abundance-only sufficiency is weakened, and PMP22 mediation is not measured. Figures 5-7 also report failed single-branch rescues. Source authors interpret parallel nonredundant pathways; this audit distinguishes that interpretation from unidentified quantitative PMP22 mediation.

